Goal / Purpose
The MEAL TL is the focal point for collecting and documentation monitoring, evaluation, accountability, and learning information at the base level.
He/she supports the programme teams through monitoring, data collection, data processing, mapping, and information analysis.
S/he will coordinate with PMs and FCs to highlight the key issues related to program quality and relevancy captured through MEAL mechanism (either through field monitoring or studies), their course correction and recommendations for future improvement.
S/he will support MEAL Coordination in organizing MEAL capacity building events for both MEAL and program staff.
List of Tasks and Responsibilities
Monitoring and Evaluation:
Ensure Field Monitoring Reports (FMRs) are generated for covered all projects and FMRs shared weekly;
Centralize / follow-up creation and update of monitoring plans;
Contribute to the revision of monitoring and evaluation tools and train program teams on design and proper use;
Participate in data analysis and writing of monitoring and evaluation reports;
Participate in the follow-up of recommendations;
Propose cross-cutting monitoring activities to improve the quality of the response;
Ensure MEAL team weekly planning and follow up;
Respect schedules and deadlines agreed upon with his/her manager;
